window.docContents[7].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.SignalSession.PqDir/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___SignalSession___PqDir":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession › PqDir.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by no headline theorem 463 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Listed with the statement files, but no headline theorem uses it. None of its declarations is in the closure of a headline theorem of either proof. Tier 1 lists it, as the closure report does: the report lists every statement file (defaultStatementFiles in scripts/TrustedClosure.lean). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (27)structure PqSignedKeystructure PqKyberKeystructure PqPartydef signedRecordBytesdef kyberRecordBytesdef oneTimeRecordBytesdef baseKeysBytesdef encodeDirdef pqInputsdef publicBundleOfdef pqInitInputsdef pqSendInputsdef pqRecvInputsdef PqParty.trustsdef pqxdhExpectedOutcomedef pqInitModeldef pqSendModeldef pqxdhSessionDecryptModeldef pqRecvWhisperModeldef preKeysNamedBydef markKyberUseddef removeOpkdef PqSessionMatchesinstance L323def pqRecvPrekeyModeldef PqxdhPartyInSpecDomaindef CliSpecPqxdh\n\n\n\nFunctional specification of the signal-session CLI on PQXDH directories: CliSpecPqxdhTrusted: the statement. Read with Run.lean and SmDir.lean (partyAddress, textBytes) to trust the PQXDH-mode CLI statements (see Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md).CliSpecPqxdh run X W specifies init, send, and recv on directories encoded (encodeDir) from a party state st : PqParty in PqxdhPartyInSpecDomain W st over model primitives W : PEParams (extern hooks in the binary: DEV-E8, DEV-PQ1) and X : UnreachedPqxdhPrimitives:* init <peer> bundle (with st.session = none): trust-on-first-use check (PqParty.trusts), then initiateState (pqInitModel).* send <peer>: messageEncrypt with SPQR V1 (pqSendModel), emitting 3 ‖ PreKeySignalMessage while unacknowledged and 2 ‖ SignalMessage thereafter, followed by the remote-identity trust check.* recv <peer> of 2 ‖ c: SignalMessage.tryFrom and tryDecryptFromRecord with .whisper (pqRecvWhisperModel).* recv <peer> of 3 ‖ m.bytes for canonical m : PreKeyMessageFields when st.session is none or matches m (PqSessionMatches): trust check, then either matching-session decryption or preKeysNamedBy + recvPrekeyState + markKyberUsed + removeOpk (pqRecvPrekeyModel, DEV-PQ8).* recv <peer> with any other leading byte or empty input: rejected with exit 1.Non-canonical pre-key encodings and calls that archive an existing session (init over an existing session or recv of a non-matching pre-key message; DEV-C-PREV) lie outside CliSpecPqxdh's domain (for non-matching pre-key recv, see PqDirNoMatch.lean). Because the CLI clock is UNIX_EPOCH and all reachable records carry timestamp 0, unacknowledged-session expiry never triggers (DEV-PQ9).\n\n\n\nA party's state\n\nstructure PqSignedKeyL53–61 ↗#A signed pre-key: its private half (the public half is derived, keyPairOf), its signature and its timestamp.\n\nstructure PqKyberKeyL63–72 ↗#A Kyber1024 pre-key: public and secret key, its signature and its timestamp.\n\nstructure PqPartyL74–93 ↗#A party's state on PQXDH directories: everything its directory holds.\n\nThe directory of a party (stores.rs)\n\ndef signedRecordBytesL97–101 ↗#The record of a signed pre-key with id id (SignedPreKeyRecord::serialize): id, the serialized public key (derived from the private key), the private key, signature, timestamp.\n\ndef kyberRecordBytesL103–107 ↗#The record of a Kyber pre-key with id id (KyberPreKeyRecord::serialize): keys behind type byte 0x08.\n\ndef oneTimeRecordBytesL109–113 ↗#The record of a one-time pre-key with id id (PreKeyRecord::serialize).\n\ndef baseKeysBytesL115–117 ↗#The .base-keys file of a last-resort Kyber pre-key: signed id:u32 ‖ base key[33] each.\n\ndef encodeDirL119–144 ↗#The files of a party's directory (paths relative to it):* address (text), identity-key-pair (IdentityKeyPair::serialize: the public key derived from the private key, and the private key), registration-id (u32 little-endian);* identities/<peer name>: the peer's pinned identity key, if any;* sessions/<peer address>: the session's record (encodeRecordUnderExtras), if any;* each signed pre-key, one-time pre-key and one-time Kyber pre-key record (an empty file when used), each last-resort Kyber pre-key record and its .base-keys file (always written). The directories are partyDirs.\n\ndef pqInputsL146–153 ↗#The inputs of one call of the party st with command cmd: its directory, the files extra (the bundle directory for init), the coins file coins, and stdin stdin.\n\ndef publicBundleOfL155–161 ↗#The bundle directory's contents for a typed bundle (public.rs): keys serialized behind their type bytes.\n\ndef pqInitInputsL163–168 ↗#init <peer> bundle by st with the typed bundle b in the bundle directory and the 192 coin bytes t.\n\ndef pqSendInputsL170–173 ↗#send <peer> of plaintext m by st with the 64 coin bytes r.\n\ndef pqRecvInputsL175–178 ↗#recv <peer> of the message c (type byte included) by st with the 32 bytes of the receive coins rc.\n\nEach call's outcome in the model\n\ndef PqParty.trustsL182–187 ↗#The trust check (is_trusted_identity, trust on first use): no pinned key, or the pinned key is k.\n\ndef pqxdhExpectedOutcomeL189–195 ↗#The run's outcome for the model's answer r on the inputs i of the party W-encoded from st: none = panic (abort); some none = rejection (exit 1, files unchanged); some (some (st', out)) = acceptance: exit 0, stdout out, and the files i.files overwritten by the new directory encodeDir W st'.\n\ndef pqInitModelL197–205 ↗#init's model (process_prekey_bundle): the trust check of the bundle's identity key, then initiateState (the bundle's signatures, PQXDH, the initiator session; null on any failure); on success the peer's identity key is pinned and the session stored. Never panics.\n\ndef pqSendModelL207–230 ↗#send's model (message_encrypt): no session rejects; else the session model's messageEncrypt with V1 SPQR, the party's address blob and the coins r (panic aborts, other errors reject), then the trust check of the session's remote identity. On success the new session (same extras) and the remote identity pinned; stdout 3 ‖ firstMessageBody while unacknowledged, else 2 ‖ SignalMessage, as sendWireModel.\n\ndef pqxdhSessionDecryptModelL232–250 ↗#The receiving session's outcome for a parsed SignalMessage msg of type ty on the session (x, g) (decrypt_message_with_record on a record without previous sessions): the session model's tryDecryptFromRecord (the party's expected addresses, coins rc; panic aborts, other errors reject), then the trust check of the remote identity; on success the new session (same extras, ghost state otherwise unchanged) and the plaintext.\n\ndef pqRecvWhisperModelL253–262 ↗#recv's model on 2 ‖ c (message_decrypt_signal): no session rejects; c that does not parse (SignalMessage::try_from) rejects; else pqxdhSessionDecryptModel with type Whisper.\n\ndef preKeysNamedByL264–291 ↗#The pre-keys a pre-key message m names, from st's stores, as ResponderPreKeySecrets (none: one is missing, so libsignal rejects):* the signed pre-key m.spkId (get_signed_pre_key);* the Kyber pre-key m.kpkId (get_kyber_pre_key): the one-time key if its file is not empty, else the last-resort key with that id;* the one-time pre-key m.opkId, if m names one (get_pre_key): a used (empty) one is missing.\n\ndef markKyberUsedL293–309 ↗#mark_kyber_pre_key_used(m.kpkId, m.spkId, m.baseKey) on st's stores (none: the store refuses, so libsignal rejects): a one-time Kyber pre-key whose file is not empty is emptied; else the last-resort key m.kpkId refuses when its .base-keys replay list exceeds fileCapBytes (37 * seen.length > fileCapBytes, where Dir::get / readFileHook returns Err) or holds the (signed pre-key id, base key) pair (\"reused base key\"), and otherwise appends it.\n\ndef removeOpkL311–315 ↗#remove_pre_key(m.opkId), if m names a one-time pre-key: its file is emptied.\n\ndef PqSessionMatchesL317–321 ↗#The session (x, g) matches the pre-key message m (promote_matching_session on the current session): its alice_base_key is m's base key, serialized, and its version is m's (currentVersion, the high nibble of m.bytes's first byte).\n\ninstanceL323–325 ↗#\n\ndef pqRecvPrekeyModelL327–373 ↗#recv's model on 3 ‖ m.bytes for a typed pre-key message m (message_decrypt_prekey):1. m.inner that does not parse (SignalMessage::try_from) rejects (PreKeySignalMessage:: try_from parses it);2. the trust check of m's identity key (process_prekey);3. with a session that matches m (PqSessionMatches; promote_matching_session): the session's remote identity must be m's identity key, then the session's tryDecryptFromRecord with type PreKey; no pre-key is used;4. with no session: preKeysNamedBy (a missing pre-key rejects), recvPrekeyState (PQXDH, the recipient session, the first decryption; panic aborts), markKyberUsed (a refusal — missing key, last-resort .base-keys above fileCapBytes, or replayed base key — rejects with exit 1 and files unchanged), then removeOpk;5. on success m's identity key is pinned and the session stored; stdout is the plaintext. A session that does not match m is outside CliSpecPqxdh's domain (libsignal would archive it, and encodeRecordUnderExtras writes no previous sessions: DEV-C-PREV); the model then rejects.\n\nThe domain and the spec\n\ndef PqxdhPartyInSpecDomainL377–406 ↗#The party states CliSpecPqxdh covers (the games keep their parties in it):* a session, if any, encodes as a reachable one (ReachablePqxdhSession: a PQXDH handshake started it and the wire entries continued it) for st's identity: some reachable g₀ has the same party and session state, is st.party's, and its record is below 2^31 bytes (the bound ReachablePqxdhSession's steps carry);* every file of the directory is below 2^31 bytes, and every file other than a last-resort .base-keys file (baseKeysFile i) is at most fileCapBytes (2^21) bytes;* the pre-key ids of each kind are distinct (each names one file).DEV-CLI21 (libsignal): bounded I/O caps and stated last-resort .base-keys cap rejection (effect: none). Each CLI run enforces the bounded-read I/O caps (stdinCapBytes = 2^20, fileCapBytes = 2^21, cliPathMaxBytes = 4096) and refuses send plaintext above maxPlaintextBytes (1_000_000) with exit 1. In PqxdhPartyInSpecDomain and markKyberUsed: (i) non-.base-keys files are at most fileCapBytes (ReachablePqxdhSession records are ≤ 1,209,331 B; other store files are fixed-size), while .base-keys (baseKeysFile i) stays below 2^31 bytes; (ii) the .base-keys read cap (37 * seen.length > fileCapBytes in markKyberUsed, from the 56,681-st handshake on one unrotated last-resort key) is a modelled exit-1 rejection with files unchanged; (iii) cliPqExp never reaches that rejection (seen.length ≤ 1).The session conjunct ignores ghost epochs (GhostState.epoch, chainEpochs), which are not serialized by encodeRecordUnderExtras.\n\ndef CliSpecPqxdhL408–464 ↗#The CLI on PQXDH directories (run is any implementation; the real one is the engine process of the CLI's ELF). For every model primitives W and model extras X, every party state st in the domain (PqxdhPartyInSpecDomain), and each call below, standard input above stdinCapBytes (2^20) exits 2 (read_stdin cap), send plaintext above maxPlaintextBytes (10^6) exits 1 before running the model (with every file unchanged in both cases), and otherwise the run's outcome is the model's (pqxdhExpectedOutcome):1. init <peer> bundle with no session (DEV-C-PREV), any typed bundle b and the 192 coin bytes t: pqInitModel;2. send <peer> of any plaintext m below 2^32 bytes with the 64 coin bytes r: exit 2 if m.length > stdinCapBytes, else exit 1 if m.length > maxPlaintextBytes, else pqSendModel;3. recv <peer> of 2 ‖ c for any c below 2^32 bytes, with coins rc: exit 2 if (2 ‖ c).length > stdinCapBytes, else pqRecvWhisperModel;4. recv <peer> of 3 ‖ m.bytes for a typed pre-key message m (other encodings are outside the domain) whose inner message is below 2^32 - 2048 bytes, when there is no session or the session matches m (DEV-C-PREV), with coins rc: exit 2 if (3 ‖ m.bytes).length > stdinCapBytes, else pqRecvPrekeyModel;5. recv <peer> of any input below 2^32 bytes whose first byte is neither 2 nor 3, or of nothing: exit 2 if c.length > stdinCapBytes, else exit 1, with every file unchanged. In 1–4 m's registration id, ids, keys and inner message are any values (the adversary's).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/SignalSession/PqDir.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.SignalSession.PqDir/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___SignalSession___PqDir"}});